==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|trecheros|lang=fro}}, {{term|tricheros||deceitful|lang=fro}}. See [[treacher]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtɹetʃəɹəs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-treacherous.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Exhibiting [[treachery]].
# [[deceitful|Deceitful]]; inclined to [[betray]].
# [[unreliable|Unreliable]]; [[dangerous]].
#: ''a '''treacherous''' mountain trail''

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|exhibiting treachery}} [[loyal]]

